<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14730" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dŏnax</span></b> , ăcis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόναξ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A sort of reed</i> or <i>cane</i>,
				<i>Cyprus-reed</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				36, 66, § 165</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 11, 50, §
			86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 10, 52,
				§ 141</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sea-fish</i> = solen, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32,
				11, 53, § 151</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The male scallop</i> or <i>pecten</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 9, 32, §
			103</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dŏnax</span></b> , <i>a Greek proper name</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun. 4,
				7, 2</span></i>, and 4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>